Participation is voluntary. A person should know who can access a contribution and why, and should have a clear way to decline, pause, withdraw it, or leave. Membership does not grant access to another participant's vault, accounts, devices, or data. Shared decisions do not transfer ownership of private writing without separate permission.

## possible contents

- participation, moderation, decision-making, appeal, and exit rules;
- a map of groups, projects, and offers, only with participant consent;
- shared methods and modules linked to the open system;
- agreements on collaboration, authorship, licenses, and responsibilities;
- meeting notes only by agreement and with a defined retention period;
- technical designs after a threat model and independent review.

